  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "sXKHLzqy//BHm8tC9QkfqTshF7A=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:27:29.016Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The record for cbs Corporate Business Solutions has been corrected: it was listed as independent and is in fact wholly owned by Materna Group, and has been since 2005. This is not a recent change that the research missed by a few months \u2014 it is a two-decade-old fact that the original row got wrong.\n\nIndependence is a live scoring dimension in this corpus, not a descriptive nicety. Sibling rows are flagged specifically for leaving or growing the independent pool when they change hands, so a firm's independence status feeds directly into how it is ranked and approached. Moving cbs from independent to wholly-owned subsidiary changes the level at which a platform decision would be taken.\n\nIts recorded stack reinforces the point. SAP sits at the core with SecurityBridge alongside, serving manufacturing, pharma, automotive and life science, which is a fully occupied platform slot by the standards of the mechanical size-and-slot-occupancy rescore this row received. The flag still calls for an OSS-portfolio screen before anything is acted on, and the corrected ownership is one more reason to run it.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**4 \u00b7 needs OSS screen**\n- cbs Corporate Business Solutions (DE)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> \u26a0 CORRECTION (Owner): was Independent \u2192 now MATERNA GROUP, wholly owned since 2005. DERIVED, NOT SCORED ON v3 \u2014 v2 row rescored mechanically (size + slot-occupancy only). Run the OSS-portfolio screen before acting. v2 verticals: Manufacturing, pharma, automotive, life science",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:27:29.016247Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:27:29.016252Z"
    }
  },
